        "title": "Best time to visit around 5pm",
        "text": "Every evening after sunset there is a special puja held - Arati. Hindu priest are singing and dancing with fire lamps. Even these days the dead are rarely burned at the riverside, but in a new electric oven, still it is a place to be reminded that we all are going to die one day. Behind the river you will find a big ground with trees and temples, a place to meditate and find calm within that busy city. The main Hindu temple cannot be visited inside by visitors, only Hindus can enter. Respect the place and dress accordingly!",
