        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r550538727-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Profound experience",
        "text": "I visited two years ago, and the spiritual and philosophical experience of watching the cremation ceremony still stays with me. It's not for everyone, but I was deeply moved by the proceedings, and the many people, both locals and foreign visitors, seated on the opposite bank contemplating the ongoing ceremonies. \n\nThe temple compound itself was beautiful, though a big part of it was only open to Hindus for praying. I think that's fair enough, respecting that this was foremost a place of worship. However, the entrance fee for foreign visitors should be correspondingly lowered in my opinion. \n\nThe stagnant river into which the ashes were swept into was putrid, and people seemed indifferent to it. I wonder if it was for religious reasons that it wasn't cleaned and managed better, or simply negligence.",
