      {
        "review_id": 549748977,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r549748977-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Culturally interesting, but a little invasive",
        "text": "I wish I could say that Pashupatinath was a highlight of the trip – it is a really important Hindu temple and it was on our must-do list – but it wasn't my FAVORITE part of the trip.  On the upside, it was huge and there were plenty of places to explore.  On the downside, it felt a little invasive and inappropriate to be exploring around people's personal funerals and cremations, and seeing people photographing these things.  If you're looking for culture, you'll definitely get a different side of it here so I would still suggest going.  But I would also just suggest keeping your distance from families who are saying goodbye to their loved ones out of respect!  Also, there are lots of men dressed as Hindu holy men who charge you for a photo and to be \"blessed.\"  Don't fall for this...it's just a way to get money from you!",
        "review_tip": null,
