      {
        "review_id": 549681616,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r549681616-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Lots of history and cultural significance if you're willing to pay the price",
        "text": "Upon arriving at Pashupatinath Temple, my fiancé and I were told the entrance fee was 1,000 rupees. While this is a bit steep in my opinion, we decided to pay the price (doubting that we would ever be back in Kathmandu to see it). After buying our tickets and entering the temple, one of the tour guides began to explain about the historical and religious significance of the temple grounds, architecture, and open air cremations. Although we hadn't asked for a guided tour, we naively assumed that it was included in the price of the ticket. The tour guide was quite thorough and took us around the temple for about 30 minutes, offering to take our photo at certain spots along the way. You can take photos with the face-painted holy men around the temple (for a price) but we decided not to exploit the religious aspects of the temple by taking advantage of the photo ops. At the end of our tour, our tour guide explicitly asked us for a tip equal to the price of one admission ticket. Feeling somewhat duped, we abided his request. \nTake aways: If you don't want to pay extra, you should explicitly state that you don't want a guided tour. The tour does offer you many bits of information that you won't get otherwise so keep that in mind.\nThe site is rich with Hindu culture and history and well worth the ticket price in my opinion.\nBe respectful. Real people come to this site 24 hours a day to cremate their loved ones. Don't be intrusive and respect their privacy.",
